  <h2>Notes from the review</h2>
  <p class="lead">Read-only review — nothing was changed in Tern. Per the Key Rules, any change here goes to Barbara first.</p>
  <div class="notes"><ul><li><b>Auto-Apply</b> 5 of 13 Workflows apply themselves: Payment Reminders, Booked | Trip Status, Hotel Only (add research and concierge fee to task templates), Premium/Lux Cruise BOOKED Workflow MC, Client Care | Important Dates. The rest are added to a trip by hand. FIT | Planning to Booked, Trips | Planning, Concierge (hotel only), WWT Premium/Lux Cruise and Trip Status - Hotel Only have a trigger saved but Auto-Apply switched off.</li><li><b>Inactive automations</b> 22 of 59 automations are Inactive, so they stay in the Workflow but won’t send until switched on after the Workflow is applied: Trips | Planning (2); FIT | Planning to Booked (4); Payment Reminders (3); Hotel Only (add research and concierge fee to task templates) (2); Mass Market Cruise BOOKED Workflow MC (2); Premium/Lux Cruise BOOKED Workflow MC (6); WWT Premium/Lux Cruise BOOKED Workflow MC (3). Many are set up that way on purpose (“personalize & activate”).</li><li><b>Quiet stages</b> No active automated client email runs during: Inquiry &amp; lead, Discovery &amp; engagement, Traveling. Inquiry and discovery are handled with Tasks and manual templates today.</li><li><b>Same tag, two Workflows</b> Premium/Lux Cruise BOOKED Workflow MC and WWT Premium/Lux Cruise BOOKED Workflow MC both listen for the “Prem/Lux River” trip tag. Only the original MC version has Auto-Apply on, so the tag adds that one.</li><li><b>Status updates in two places</b> The Traveling and Traveled status updates appear in Booked | Trip Status, Hotel Only, and Trip Status - Hotel Only (marked “temp do not apply”).</li><li><b>Automation emails are copies</b> Emails inside automations are their own copies. Editing a library template does not change the automation version, and the reverse. 41 of 56 library templates are sent manually only.</li><li><b>Forms not linked anywhere</b> 5 forms aren’t attached to an email template or automation: Authorization, Hotel Reservation Confirmation, Client Inquiry form, Copy of Trip Inquiry Form, Travel Insurance Decline Waiver. The two inquiry forms sit in a folder named “Delete”.</li><li><b>Small tidy-ups</b> “Payment Reminder TBD” is timed for the day the trip starts. “Lead Task List (Trip basis)” has a status trigger with no status chosen. The library template named “New Email Template” was written for one client’s trip and could be renamed or archived.</li><li><b>Couldn’t verify</b> Form response counts for forms inside folders, and the “source” of the MC cruise set (inferred from names). Auto-Apply on/off is taken from the Workflows list.</li><li><b>Possible overlap</b> The three cruise Workflows share most of their emails and Tasks. A duplicate review would show which one to keep as the main version.</li></ul></div>
  <div class="take"><h3>Key takeaway</h3>The booked and pre-trip journey is well built out, especially for cruises and hotel-only trips, and Client Care keeps relationships warm all year. Open decisions for Barbara: which cruise Workflow is the main one, whether to turn on Auto-Apply where it’s saved but off, and whether to add a light automated touch to the inquiry and discovery stages.</div>
